WEBVTT

00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:03.634
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.620
<v><b>Stella:</b></v> <i>Dune</i> is on Netflix now. Have you seen it?

00:00:12.027 --> 00:00:15.330
<v><b>Paul:</b></v> The new one that won a lot of Oscars not so long ago?

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.154
Yes, I have!

00:00:17.647 --> 00:00:18.993
And I’ve read the book.

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:23.272
The book’s better than the movie, I think. It’s a classic!

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:27.997
<v><b>Stella:</b></v> Would you mind watching it again with me? I really want to see it.

00:00:29.518 --> 00:00:30.172
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:32.823 --> 00:00:35.604
<v><b>Matt:</b></v> Have you read the Sherlock Holmes books?

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:38.152
<v><b>Tom:</b></v> No, I haven’t.

00:00:38.794 --> 00:00:42.773
There are so many of them! Life’s too short!

00:00:43.459 --> 00:00:45.085
<v><b>Matt:</b></v> Have you watched <i>Sherlock</i>?

00:00:45.518 --> 00:00:51.428
<v><b>Tom:</b></v> Yes, I’ve watched the first three seasons, and I’ve downloaded the fourth.

00:00:55.244 --> 00:00:55.885
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:02.912
<v><b>Lexi:</b></v> Have you seen <i>Les Misérables</i>? The musical, I mean.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:09.403
<v><b>Mason:</b></v> I’ve seen the movie, but I haven’t seen it at the theater. I’d love to go.

00:01:09.889 --> 00:01:11.335
<v><b>Lexi:</b></v> Let’s get tickets.

00:01:11.745 --> 00:01:14.358
I’ve read the book and I love the music!